                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Titanis is the kind of game you play during a rainy afternoon, when you want to kill a couple of hours and you don't feel like doing something meaningful with your life. It doesn't excel in anything but it's not a bad game either; it's relaxing and casual but at the same time I didn't find it boring at all; truth is I was planning to give it a try for 15-30 minutes but I ended up playing 4-5 hours until I managed to unlock the whole content.\n\nTitanis is a side scrolling action game with some platforming bits and a few RPG elements. There's not much story attached to it though - the protagonist Bash takes up a mission to fight the strange creatures attacking a settlement in the middle of the desert. \n\nThe levels consist mainly of killing the enemies and completing some objectives. Those  award money and skill points that you can further use to upgrade your armor or unlock new skills. With a total of 16 skills of which you can equip 4 at the same time, there's not much variety of spells, but on the other hand, the enemies are so easy to kill that you don't really need to use more than a basic damage attack 2 or 3 times for a given mob to be dead. The only moments in which you need to use more than 1 skill are the two boss fights you encounter. While the game seemed to me like a walk in the park, the last boss proved to be rather difficult compared to everything else before, even with all the upgrades and skills unlocked, and I had to retry the level quite a few times before I  managed to beat it.\n\nAchievement-wise, this is not an easy 100% despite the fact that it seems to be so, judging by the difficulty of the levels. Don't be fooled by the \"Beat the boss without taking damage.\" achievements - while one of those 2 is doable after a little practice and by spamming shields non stop and dodging everything, the other one is much much harder.\n\nThis is a short game that you can play in one setting, but the replayability is enhanced by the inclusion of the level editor.\n\n[quote]More reviews on the [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/11354094]Lilly's Corner Curator page[/url][/quote]",
